    "known_limitations": "Every constant here is declared judgement, not measurement: fineness ratio, packing efficiency, areal densities, specific power, the systems and gear fractions. No structural fuselage sizing -- the shell is weighed by area, not sized against loads, so a pressurised or highly loaded body would be understated. No margin policy and no growth allowance, which real programmes carry at 5-10%. SEPARATELY, this module can also produce the non-wing parasite drag the aero publications currently carry as a declared constant (0.0062 + 0.14/S_ref). The wetted-area build-up gives roughly 35-50% LESS than that constant (S=10,W0=500: 0.01234, S=16,W0=700: 0.01002, S=22,W0=1100: 0.00898), i.e. a clean-configuration estimate. The truth is probably between the two and the discrepancy is an open item for review -- aero has NOT yet been switched over to it."
